---

## 5) Extended Standard Library

- **core commands**: `echo`, `pwd`, `cd`, `ls`, `cat`, `typeof`
- **process exec**: `!cmd` runs external commands (like Bash)
- **math**: `+ - * / % pow sqrt`
- **array**: `map`, `filter`, `reduce`
- **option/result**: `map`, `unwrap`, `unwrap_or`
- **pattern match** integrated for Option/Result.

---

## 6) Examples

### 6.1 Arithmetic & lambdas

```au
let xs = [1,2,3,4]
xs |> map(|x: Int| x * x) |> echo
```

### 6.2 Pattern matching

```au
let resp = http.get("https://api.example.com")
match resp.status {
  200 => echo("ok"),
  404 => echo("not found"),
  n if n >= 500 => echo("server error: ${n}"),
  _ => echo("other status")
}
```

### 6.3 Type error detection

```au
let x: Int = "hello"   # compile-time error
```

### 6.4 Operator pipelines

```au
ls(".") |> take(5) |> echo
```

### 6.5 External command runner (Bash vibe)

```au
!git status
```

---

## 7) Code organization

We now provide a **compile‑ready, modular project** that:

- Uses `|` for pipelines.
- Supports **Go‑like `:=` inference**, optional `let` annotations, and **arrow lambdas** (`fn(...) => ...`).
- Adds **AI & Agent** integration with a clean trait you can implement for any provider. Default build compiles **without** network access (no external deps). Enable `--features ai-openai` to call a live LLM.

> Create a new cargo project `aether`, replace files below, then `cargo run`. For live AI: `cargo run --features ai-openai` with `OPENAI_API_KEY` set.

### `Cargo.toml`

```toml
[package]
name = "aether"
version = "0.4.0"
edition = "2021"

[dependencies]
anyhow = "1"
rustyline = "14"
serde = { version = "1", features = ["derive"] }
serde_json = "1"
chrono = { version = "0.4", features = ["serde"] }
walkdir = "2"
which = "6"

[features]
ai = []
ai-openai = ["ai", "reqwest/blocking", "serde", "serde_json"]

[dependencies.reqwest]
version = "0.12"
default-features = false
features = ["blocking", "json"]
```

### `src/main.rs`

```rust
mod ast;    mod lexer;  mod parser; mod types; mod typecheck;
mod value;  mod env;    mod builtins; mod eval;  mod repl;
#[cfg(feature = "ai")] mod ai;
#[cfg(feature = "ai")] mod agent;

// Entry point
fn main() -> anyhow::Result<()> { repl::start() }
```

### `src/ast.rs`

```rust
#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
pub enum Expr {
    Lit(super::value::Value),
    Var(String),
    Let { name: String, ty: Option<super::types::Type>, value: Box<Expr>, mutable: bool },
    Bind { name: String, value: Box<Expr>, mutable: bool },   // x := expr
    Call { callee: Box<Expr>, args: Vec<Expr> },
    Pipe(Box<Expr>, Box<Expr>),
    Unary { op: OpUn, rhs: Box<Expr> },
    Binary { lhs: Box<Expr>, op: OpBin, rhs: Box<Expr> },
    Lambda { params: Vec<(String, super::types::Type)>, body: Box<Expr> },
    Match { scrutinee: Box<Expr>, arms: Vec<(Pattern, Expr)> },
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
pub enum Pattern { Wild, Lit(super::value::Value), IntRange(i64,i64) }

#[derive(Copy, Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum OpUn { Neg, Not }

#[derive(Copy, Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum OpBin { Add, Sub, Mul, Div, Rem, Eq, Ne, Lt, Lte, Gt, Gte, And, Or }
```

